      // saves `readForm()` — the SUBSTITUTED state — back over the draft. So the
      // blocker appeared once, the substituted value was written into the draft,
      // and on the next load `writeForm` found it perfectly valid: reload, and
      // the red mark is gone and the export asserts a choice nobody made. That
      // is the brief's own listed bug restored one keystroke later by the commit
